  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This error seems to occur in many different ways. Once it has happened, the quick search menu is not functional (though the full search is just fine) and you have to restart unity to fix it. Not even a layout reload is able to fix it.\n\nIt can happen from several different random things. I am unsure about all of them, but the one consistent way I have found is to open a graph containing a set variable node with no reference. It's supposed to delete those types of nodes, which does happen eventually if the graph updates, but not before causing this error.",
